      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what to improve.Now I understand the test. It verifies that after setting flags to `ACCESS_TIME_BIT` (value 2, meaning only access-time bit is set), calling `getCentralDirectoryData()` does not alter the flags. I'll write a cleaner, more understandable version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces the magic number `(byte) 2` with the named constant `X5455_ExtendedTimestamp.ACCESS_TIME_BIT`, renames the variable to `extendedTimestamp` for clarity, and adds a Javadoc comment explaining the intent: verifying that `getCentralDirectoryData()` leaves the flags field unchanged when only the access-time bit is set."
